The ESM migration is written under `/output` and uses only local `.mjs` imports.

**Library Files**
- Public interface: [index.mjs](/output/lib/index.mjs:1)
- CLI: [program-name.mjs](/output/lib/cli/program-name.mjs:1), [messages.mjs](/output/lib/cli/messages.mjs:1), [parse-args.mjs](/output/lib/cli/parse-args.mjs:1)
- Bencode core: [bytes-value.mjs](/output/lib/bencode/bytes-value.mjs:1), [dict-value.mjs](/output/lib/bencode/dict-value.mjs:1), [decode-first.mjs](/output/lib/bencode/decode-first.mjs:1), [decode.mjs](/output/lib/bencode/decode.mjs:1)
- Formatting/support: [python-repr.mjs](/output/lib/format/python-repr.mjs:1), [ensure-ascii.mjs](/output/lib/text/ensure-ascii.mjs:1), [named-error.mjs](/output/lib/shared/named-error.mjs:1)

**Entry File**
- [test4.mjs](/output/test4.mjs:1)

```js
import { CliExit, decode, ensureAscii, formatPythonValue, parseArgs } from './lib/index.mjs';
import { formatPythonTraceback } from './lib/shared/named-error.mjs';

function main(argv = process.argv) {
  const { a } = parseArgs(argv);
  const result = decode(ensureAscii(a));
  console.log(formatPythonValue(result));
}

try {
  main(process.argv);
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof CliExit) {
    if (error.stdout) {
      process.stdout.write(error.stdout);
    }

    if (error.stderr) {
      process.stderr.write(error.stderr);
    }

    process.exitCode = error.exitCode;
  } else if (error && error.isPythonStyleError) {
    if (error.stdout) {
      process.stdout.write(error.stdout);
    }

    process.stderr.write(`${formatPythonTraceback(error)}\n`);
    process.exitCode = 1;
  } else {
    throw error;
  }
}
```

Verified with `node /output/test4.mjs --a 9:value`, `--a 6:mu`, `--a 10:deco`, `--a 4:dict`, `--a=value`, repeated `--a`, `--help`, missing `--a`, and nested list/dict cases. Valid-path stdout matches the executable; malformed decode errors are rendered in Python-style form, without the executable’s extra PyInstaller footer.
